168, 393, 611, 808, 337, 1017, 3278, 502, 13, 51714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31379864820793496, "compression_ratio": 1.7195571955719557, "no_speech_prob": 0.005202773492783308}, {"id": 44, "seek": 18000, "start": 207.0, "end": 209.0, "text": " How will I get the question?", "tokens": [51714, 1012, 486, 286, 483, 264, 1168, 30, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31379864820793496, "compression_ratio": 1.7195571955719557, "no_speech_prob": 0.005202773492783308}, {"id": 45, "seek": 21000, "start": 210.0, "end": 217.0, "text": " I will get the question that the size of the floor is equal to 4 cross n.", "tokens": [50364, 286, 486, 483, 264, 1168, 300, 264, 2744, 295, 264, 4123, 307, 2681, 281, 1017, 3278, 297, 13, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28288932556801655, "compression_ratio": 1.8100558659217878, "no_speech_prob": 0.002177334623411298}, {"id": 46, "seek": 21000, "start": 217.0, "end": 220.0, "text": " So, my floor will look something like this.", "tokens": [50714, 407, 11, 452, 4123, 486, 574, 746, 411, 341, 13, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28288932556801655, "compression_ratio": 1.8100558659217878, "no_speech_prob": 0.002177334623411298}, {"id": 47, "seek": 21000, "start": 220.0, "end": 225.0, "text": " This side will always be 4 and this side will always be n.", "tokens": [50864, 639, 1252, 486, 1009, 312, 1017, 293, 341, 1252, 486, 1009, 312, 297, 13, 51114], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28288932556801655, "compression_ratio": 1.8100558659217878, "no_speech_prob": 0.002177334623411298}, {"id": 48, "seek": 21000, "start": 225.0, "end": 227.0, "text": " After that, what will be the size of the tile?", "tokens": [51114, 2381, 300, 11, 437, 486, 312, 264, 2744, 295, 264, 20590, 30, 51214], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28288932556801655, "compression_ratio": 1.8100558659217878, "no_speech_prob": 0.002177334623411298}, {"id": 49, "seek": 21000, "start": 227.0, "end": 233.0, "text": " We will get the size of the tile equal to 4 cross 1.", "tokens": [51214, 492, 486, 483, 264, 2744, 295, 264, 20590, 2681, 281, 1017, 3278, 502, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28288932556801655, "compression_ratio": 1.8100558659217878, "no_speech_prob": 0.002177334623411298}, {"id": 50, "seek": 21000, "start": 233.0, "end": 236.0, "text": " So, there is no need to apply the same formula.", "tokens": [51514, 407, 11, 456, 307, 572, 643, 281, 3079, 264, 912, 8513, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.28288932556801655, "compression_ratio": 1.8100558659217878, "no_speech_prob": 0.002177334623411298}, {"id": 51, "seek": 23600, "start": 236.0, "end": 238.0, "text": " The formula will look exactly the same.", "tokens": [50364, 440, 8513, 486, 574, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 52, "seek": 23600, "start": 238.0, "end": 241.0, "text": " If you have this question for 4 cross 1, then it will also come.", "tokens": [50464, 759, 291, 362, 341, 1168, 337, 1017, 3278, 502, 11, 550, 309, 486, 611, 808, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 53, "seek": 23600, "start": 241.0, "end": 245.0, "text": " Along with this, there will be a lot of questions in the recursion,", "tokens": [50614, 17457, 365, 341, 11, 456, 486, 312, 257, 688, 295, 1651, 294, 264, 20560, 313, 11, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 54, "seek": 23600, "start": 245.0, "end": 247.0, "text": " in which one thing is used called DP.", "tokens": [50814, 294, 597, 472, 551, 307, 1143, 1219, 42796, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 55, "seek": 23600, "start": 247.0, "end": 250.0, "text": " DP means Dynamic Programming.", "tokens": [50914, 42796, 1355, 45440, 8338, 2810, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 56, "seek": 23600, "start": 250.0, "end": 255.0, "text": " Dynamic Programming means that we are solving the same question again and again.", "tokens": [51064, 45440, 8338, 2810, 1355, 300, 321, 366, 12606, 264, 912, 1168, 797, 293, 797, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 57, "seek": 23600, "start": 255.0, "end": 258.0, "text": " Instead of calculating the same thing again and again,", "tokens": [51314, 7156, 295, 28258, 264, 912, 551, 797, 293, 797, 11, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 58, "seek": 23600, "start": 258.0, "end": 259.0, "text": " what do we do?", "tokens": [51464, 437, 360, 321, 360, 30, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 59, "seek": 23600, "start": 259.0, "end": 261.0, "text": " We store the answer somewhere.", "tokens": [51514, 492, 3531, 264, 1867, 4079, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.31345085625175956, "compression_ratio": 1.7224489795918367, "no_speech_prob": 0.025756265968084335}, {"id": 60, "seek": 26100, "start": 261.0, "end": 265.0, "text": " So, here, because we have only learned basic recursion,", "tokens": [50364, 407, 11, 510, 11, 570, 321, 362, 787, 3264, 3875, 20560, 313, 11, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 61, "seek": 26100, "start": 265.0, "end": 268.0, "text": " then there will be some questions that we will solve from the recursion app,", "tokens": [50564, 550, 456, 486, 312, 512, 1651, 300, 321, 486, 5039, 490, 264, 20560, 313, 724, 11, 50714], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 62, "seek": 26100, "start": 268.0, "end": 270.0, "text": " but it will not have the most optimized solution.", "tokens": [50714, 457, 309, 486, 406, 362, 264, 881, 26941, 3827, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 63, "seek": 26100, "start": 270.0, "end": 272.0, "text": " Its time complexity will be quite large.", "tokens": [50814, 6953, 565, 14024, 486, 312, 1596, 2416, 13, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 64, "seek": 26100, "start": 272.0, "end": 275.0, "text": " So, when we go to the end and learn Dynamic Programming,", "tokens": [50914, 407, 11, 562, 321, 352, 281, 264, 917, 293, 1466, 45440, 8338, 2810, 11, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 65, "seek": 26100, "start": 275.0, "end": 279.0, "text": " after that we can solve all these questions in a maximum optimized way.", "tokens": [51064, 934, 300, 321, 393, 5039, 439, 613, 1651, 294, 257, 6674, 26941, 636, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 66, "seek": 26100, "start": 279.0, "end": 283.0, "text": " Till then, we have to wait a little because we are only working on the logic building,", "tokens": [51264, 20227, 550, 11, 321, 362, 281, 1699, 257, 707, 570, 321, 366, 787, 1364, 322, 264, 9952, 2390, 11, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 67, "seek": 26100, "start": 283.0, "end": 285.0, "text": " we are building the logic of the recursion.", "tokens": [51464, 321, 366, 2390, 264, 9952, 295, 264, 20560, 313, 13, 51564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 68, "seek": 26100, "start": 285.0, "end": 287.0, "text": " So, we are not doing the most optimized solution.", "tokens": [51564, 407, 11, 321, 366, 406, 884, 264, 881, 26941, 3827, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 69, "seek": 26100, "start": 287.0, "end": 290.0, "text": " We are learning the recursion now that how is the recursion working?", "tokens": [51664, 492, 366, 2539, 264, 20560, 313, 586, 300, 577, 307, 264, 20560, 313, 1364, 30, 51814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2956302040501645, "compression_ratio": 1.9933774834437086, "no_speech_prob": 0.1754981130361557}, {"id": 70, "seek": 29000, "start": 290.0, "end": 292.0, "text": " We have understood the logic of the recursion.", "tokens": [50364, 492, 362, 7320, 264, 9952, 295, 264, 20560, 313, 13, 50464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 71, "seek": 29000, "start": 292.0, "end": 294.0, "text": " So, the questions of the graph will be very easy.", "tokens": [50464, 407, 11, 264, 1651, 295, 264, 4295, 486, 312, 588, 1858, 13, 50564], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 72, "seek": 29000, "start": 294.0, "end": 296.0, "text": " The questions of the linked list will be very easy.", "tokens": [50564, 440, 1651, 295, 264, 9408, 1329, 486, 312, 588, 1858, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 73, "seek": 29000, "start": 296.0, "end": 298.0, "text": " There will be a lot more things that will be easy.", "tokens": [50664, 821, 486, 312, 257, 688, 544, 721, 300, 486, 312, 1858, 13, 50764], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 74, "seek": 29000, "start": 298.0, "end": 300.0, "text": " In fact, the concept of Dynamic Programming,", "tokens": [50764, 682, 1186, 11, 264, 3410, 295, 45440, 8338, 2810, 11, 50864], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 75, "seek": 29000, "start": 300.0, "end": 303.0, "text": " we will be understanding that very well in the end.", "tokens": [50864, 321, 486, 312, 3701, 300, 588, 731, 294, 264, 917, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 76, "seek": 29000, "start": 303.0, "end": 306.0, "text": " So, right now, the most optimized solution may not be available to you.", "tokens": [51014, 407, 11, 558, 586, 11, 264, 881, 26941, 3827, 815, 406, 312, 2435, 281, 291, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 77, "seek": 29000, "start": 306.0, "end": 308.0, "text": " There are a lot of problems.", "tokens": [51164, 821, 366, 257, 688, 295, 2740, 13, 51264], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 78, "seek": 29000, "start": 308.0, "end": 310.0, "text": " But yes, you will get the most logical solution.", "tokens": [51264, 583, 2086, 11, 291, 486, 483, 264, 881, 14978, 3827, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}, {"id": 79, "seek": 29000, "start": 310.0, "end": 313.0, "text": " How to understand them, how to visualize them.", "tokens": [51364, 1012, 281, 1223, 552, 11, 577, 281, 23273, 552, 13, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.34876842353180165, "compression_ratio": 1.8888888888888888, "no_speech_prob": 0.05628722161054611}], "language": "English"}